actice is often hindered by the need for extensive feature and reward engineering. Deep reinforcement learning methods can remove the need for explicit engineering of policy or value features but still require a manually specified reward function. Inverse reinforcement learning holds the promise of automatic reward acquisition, but has proven exceptionally difficult to apply to large, high-dimensional problems with unknown dynamics. In this work, we propose AIRL, a practical and scalable inverse reinforcement learning algorithm based on an adversarial reward learning formulation that is competitive with direct imitation learning algorithms. Additionally, we show that AIRL is able to recover portable reward functions that are robust to changes in dynamics, enabling us to learn policies even under significant variation in the environment seen during training. "}]}, "likes": 1, "private": false, "downloads": 1, "tags": ["transformers", "pytorch", "tensorboard", "safetensors", "bart", "text2text-generation", "generated_from_trainer", "dataset:scitldr", "license:apache-2.0", "endpoints_compatible", "region:us"], "library_name": "transformers", "createdAt": "2022-10-15T18:17:40.000Z", "modelId": "RamAnanth1/distilbart-cnn-12-6-finetuned-scitldr"}, {"_id": "65f8f14bc8f264ce4dcd9f4e", "id": "pkbiswas/Llama-2-7b-Summarization-QLoRa", "cardData": {"library_name": "peft", "tags": ["generated_from_trainer"], "datasets": ["scitldr"], "base_model": "meta-llama/Llama-2-7b-hf", "model-index": [{"name": "Llama-Summarization", "results": []}], "pipeline_tag": "summarization"}, "likes": 0, "private": false, "downloads": 1, "tags": ["peft", "safetensors", "generated_from_trainer", "summarization", "dataset:scitldr", "base_model:meta-llama/Llama-2-7b-hf", "base_model:adapter:meta-llama/Llama-2-7b-hf", "region:us"], "pipeline_tag": "summarization", "library_name": "peft", "createdAt": "2024-03-19T01:58:35.000Z", "modelId": "pkbiswas/Llama-2-7b-Summarization-QLoRa"}, {"_id": "65f90daed2ce